Introduction
If you’re a full‑stack engineer responsible for a Node.js‑powered API, you’ve probably felt the sting of a slow endpoint at least once. In production, a few milliseconds of latency can translate into lost revenue, higher cloud bills, and frustrated users. This tutorial walks you through concrete, low‑risk steps you can take today to squeeze speed out of your service: caching the right data, indexing your database, and embracing async patterns and queues. All examples use plain Node.js (no framework magic) so you can copy‑paste them into any codebase. Before you start optimizing, you need a baseline. Enable request timing in your Express (or Fastify) middleware. Log the duration and the route name. Correlate those logs with DB query times and external HTTP calls.
